1. Removed all Jest-related mocking (`jest.mock()` calls)
2. Created direct component mocks using regular React components
3. Created a mock context provider in case it's needed
4. Simplified the import error handling
5. Added more structured fallback content
6. Kept the Suspense wrapper for handling the lazy loading

This should resolve the "jest is not defined" error since we're no longer trying to use Jest mocking in a non-test environment. The component should now render properly with the mock components and utilities.

